From: "Barak A. Pearlmutter" <barak+git@pearlmutter.net>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 16:30:26 +0100
Subject: Fix: same words in the same places, extracted in a different order

Rewriting a PDF 1.4 file as PDF 1.7 with Ghostscript
(gs -sDEVICE=pdfwrite -dCompatibilityLevel=1.7 ...) moves its text by up
to a few thousandths of a point, enough to change Poppler's
reading-order reconstruction on some pages: e.g., two numerators of
displayed fractions whose tops differ by 0.001pt swap places.  Words and
Characters modes compare the words in Poppler's order, so such pages
were reported as different although their words and positions were the
same: 7 of 140 pages of one technical report.

When the word sequences differ, comparePagePair() now also checks
whether every word has a word with the same text whose bounding box is
within 0.1pt of its own, and reports no textual difference if so.  Text
that really moved, such as a reflowed paragraph, is still compared by
sequence, so reflowing alone is still not a difference and changed words
still are.  On one such page, before and after rewriting, disparPDFc now
says "documents are the same" in Words and Characters modes, where it
said "documents differ at page: 1".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DFo7ywK1YasqiQ8A3v7kVX
